# Feature Architecture - ToolkitAnalytics

## System Architecture Impact
`ToolkitAnalytics` coordinates routing telemetry data through adapters, enforcing privacy restrictions.

```mermaid
graph TD
    Trigger[SDK Consumer / Auto-Instrumentation] --> Router[ToolkitAnalytics Router]
    Router --> ConsentCheck{Consent Granted?}
    
    ConsentCheck -- Yes --> ActiveAdapters[Active Adapters: Mixpanel, PostHog, Custom...]
    ConsentCheck -- Pending --> Buffer[Disk Buffer Queue]
    ConsentCheck -- No / Denied --> Discard[Discard Event / Purge Buffer]
    
    Buffer -- setConsent(granted: true) --> ActiveAdapters
    ActiveAdapters --> Net[ToolkitNetworking Manager]
```

## Key Components
- **`AnalyticsRouter`**: Coordinates event dispatching, consent enforcement, and queue flushes.
- **`AnalyticsAdapter` Protocol**: Interface for wrapping external services (PostHog, Amplitude, etc.).
- **`DiskBufferQueue`**: Handles serializing events to a secure sandbox file.
- **`PerformanceSwizzler`**: Leverages Objective-C runtime class mutations to automatically intercept UI events.
